---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---
<BaseLayout title="Ironfeast · Building Digital Empires">
  <div class="hero">
    <section class="hero-left">
      <h1>Building Digital Empires</h1>
      <p class="sub">Gaming & Community</p>
      <a class="cta" href="/gaming/">Explore Gaming</a>
    </section>
    <section class="hero-right">
      <h1>Securing Digital Infrastructure</h1>
      <p class="sub">Open Source & Research</p>
      <a class="cta" href="/labs/">Explore Labs</a>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="about container">
    <h2>About</h2>
    <div class="about-body">
      <p>Ironfeast is more than a name; it is a digital production and engineering entity dedicated to the art of systemic mastery. While the digital landscape is crowded, we occupy a specific niche. We are not a comic book hero, nor a lifestyle brand; we are the architects of complex environments. From the logistical depth of Workers & Resources: Soviet Republic to the intricate automation of Factorio, our history is one of constant evolution—moving from reflexive action to cerebral engineering.</p>

      <p>Today, Ironfeast serves as a dual-purpose hub where gaming and infrastructure collide. We apply the same rigorous logic to building digital empires as we do to securing global software supply chains. Whether we are optimizing a manufacturing loop in Anno 117 or solving the "last-mile" incompatibility between Nix and Kubernetes, our mission remains the same: Precision, Optimization, and Community.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
